b86ec30749e42abc0af223cfd2c1783818f78d4","quote":"For the three and six months ended June 30, 2026 and 2025, substantially all of the Company’s revenue was generated in the United States.","context":"Revenue by Geography","section":"","block":99,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001856314-26-000042","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001856314","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1856314/000185631426000042/you-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/5f8b5338705ee78aac48fa88df4e6c1a7b23c18b61812cbe1239d559539722d0.bin","sha256":"5f8b5338705ee78aac48fa88df4e6c1a7b23c18b61812cbe1239d559539722d0"}},{"id":"bff2592a04a2a264344fddb9e593882cf6fc7fd74177fcf5fdd6ef1b8e116448","quote":"19. Segment Information","context":"In addition, the Credit Agreement contains certain other covenants (none of which relate to financial condition), events of default and other customary provisions. As of June 30, 2026, the Company was in compliance with all of the financial and non-financial covenants of the Credit Agreement.","section":"","block":281,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001856314-26-000042","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001856314","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1856314/000185631426000042/you-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/5f8b5338705ee78aac48fa88df4e6c1a7b23c18b61812cbe1239d559539722d0.bin","sha256":"5f8b5338705ee78aac48fa88df4e6c1a7b23c18b61812cbe1239d559539722d0"}},{"id":"901a911b554b630a9b7295c2cac3f201d5ab6f18cb9fef6feb918a9f52d54080","quote":"The Company is organized and operates as a single operating and reportable segment, which aligns with the way the Chief Operating Decision Maker (“CODM”), who is the Chief Executive Officer, evaluates financial performance and results and allocates resources based on the consolidated results of the Company as a whole. The Company's operations are primarily focused on growing and maintaining its secure identity network across multiple offerings in both aviation and non-aviation channels. See Note 1 for further information on the Company’s operations and services from which it derives its revenues.","context":"19. Segment Information","section":"","block":282,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001856314-26-000042","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001856314","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1856314/000185631426000042/you-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/5f8b5338705ee78aac48fa88df4e6c1a7b23c18b61812cbe1239d559539722d0.bin","sha256":"5f8b5338705ee78aac48fa88df4e6c1a7b23c18b61812cbe1239d559539722d0"}},{"id":"deef960b044ae5714dc4c090c00abea6a97664ba74ac661eea5f2344d7a5b4fc","quote":"Operating income and assets are managed at the consolidated level, and there are no separate components that are regularly reviewed for performance or allocation of resources. Consolidated operating income as reported in the financial statements is used by the CODM to monitor budget versus actual results, review performance and allocate resources. The Company’s condensed consolidated financial statements within this Quarterly Report on Form 10-Q reflect the Company’s operations for its single operating and reportable segment.","context":"The Company is organized and operates as a single operating and reportable segment, which aligns with the way the Chief Operating Decision Maker (“CODM”), who is the Chief Executive Officer, evaluates financial performance and results and allocates resources based on the consolidated results of the Company as a whole. The Company's operations are primarily focused on growing and maintaining its secure identity network across multiple offerings in both aviation and non-aviation channels. See Note 1 for further information on the Company’s operations and services from which it derives its revenues.","section":"","block":283,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001856314-26-000042","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001856314","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1856314/000185631426000042/you-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/5f8b5338705ee78aac48fa88df4e6c1a7b23c18b61812cbe1239d559539722d0.bin","sha256":"5f8b5338705ee78aac48fa88df4e6c1a7b23c18b61812cbe1239d559539722d0"}},{"id":"00d3693c1f7e7313e6f3f86484a364cb070c6e04797170a6ea896d04bd831723","quote":"Total revenues and long-lived assets outside of the United States are immaterial for each of the three and six months ended June 30, 2026 and 2025.","context":"Operating income and assets are managed at the consolidated level, and there are no separate components that are regularly reviewed for performance or allocation of resources. Consolidated operating income as reported in the financial statements is used by the CODM to monitor budget versus actual results, review performance and allocate resources. The Company’s condensed consolidated financial statements within this Quarterly Report on Form 10-Q reflect the Company’s operations for its single operating and reportable segment.","section":"","block":284,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001856314-26-000042","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001856314","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1856314/000185631426000042/you-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/5f8b5338705ee78aac48fa88df4e6c1a7b23c18b61812cbe1239d559539722d0.bin","sha256":"5f8b5338705ee78aac48fa88df4e6c1a7b23c18b61812cbe1239d559539722d0"}},{"id":"4f30401859c0629ea33b4a3ad6eeee6cd79c315b50aa479445d2292f3ce478f9","quote":"Clear Secure, Inc. (the “Company” or “CLEAR”) is a secure identity company making experiences safer and easier - both digitally and physically. We make everyday experiences frictionless by connecting your identity to all the things that make you, YOU - transforming the way you live, work, and travel. CLEAR has been delivering secure, frictionless experiences in airports for over 15 years, achieving exceptional user delight and trust with CLEAR+, our consumer travel subscription service. CLEAR+ enables access to predictable and fast experiences through dedicated entry lanes in airport security checkpoints nationwide. Additionally, our CLEAR Travel portfolio includes TSA PreCheck® Enrollment Provided by CLEAR, premium services such as CLEAR Concierge, other travel benefits such as expedited passport services, our free CLEAR app which helps travelers plan their trip Home to Gate, and other mobile-first identity solutions such as CLEAR ID. Our CLEAR Travel portfolio extends CLEAR’s value proposition beyond the airport lane and supports our strategy to expand use cases, increase engagement and address new customer segments such as international travelers. CLEAR1 is our business to business (“B2B”) multi-layered identity verification solution. We combine biometric, document and device signals with verified data sources to ensure users are who they claim to be. Our B2B partners can select which verification layers to deploy, based on their specific security requirements, risk tolerance and user experience goals. We partner with a breadth of organizations, with a particular focus on Healthcare, Workforce and Governmental organizations where high fidelity identity security is paramount to their operational success. Our scaled Member base and comprehensive secure identity platform underpin our CLEAR Travel and CLEAR1 businesses, maximizing security and minimizing friction for consumers and our enterprise partners.","context":"Overview","section":"ITEM 2. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":310,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001856314-26-000042","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001856314","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1856314/000185631426000042/you-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/5f8b5338705ee78aac48fa88df4e6c1a7b23c18b61812cbe1239d559539722d0.bin","sha256":"5f8b5338705ee78aac48fa88df4e6c1a7b23c18b61812cbe1239d559539722d0"}},{"id":"93b937f9cbc3c7bacce86db3922b450580e104d7374db64d4c3e41a1313186a7","quote":"22","context":"ch as CLEAR Concierge, other travel benefits such as expedited passport services, our free CLEAR app which helps travelers plan their trip Home to Gate, and other mobile-first identity solutions such as CLEAR ID. Our CLEAR Travel portfolio extends CLEAR’s value proposition beyond the airport lane and supports our strategy to expand use cases, increase engagement and address new customer segments such as international travelers. CLEAR1 is our business to business (“B2B”) multi-layered identity verification solution. We combine biometric, document and device signals with verified data sources to ensure users are who they claim to be. Our B2B partners can select which verification layers to deploy, based on their specific security requirements, risk tolerance and user experience goals. We partner with a breadth of organizations, with a particular focus on Healthcare, Workforce and Governmental organizations where high fidelity identity security is paramount to their operational success. Our scaled Member base and comprehensive secure identity platform underpin our CLEAR Travel and CLEAR1 businesses, maximizing security and minimizing friction for consumers and our enterprise partners.","section":"ITEM 2. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":311,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001856314-26-000042","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001856314","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1856314/000185631426000042/you-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/5f8b5338705ee78aac48fa88df4e6c1a7b23c18b61812cbe1239d559539722d0.bin","sha256":"5f8b5338705ee78aac48fa88df4e6c1a7b23c18b61812cbe1239d559539722d0"}}],"omittedEvidenceCount":0}},"warnings":["managementExplanations: evidence cap reached."]}